# Operation theatre UX

OT owns **surgical operational workflow**: OT scheduling/queue, procedure readiness, surgical safety, procedure state, surgeon/anaesthesia, implants/IOL, consumable/implant scan, surgical documentation, recovery handoff, finalization/cancellation, OT reporting.

Canonical board: `/dashboard/ip-management/operation-theatre` with `IpSlotBoard`, `OtSurgicalSafetyChecklist`, `ImplantScanPanel`, `AnaesthesiaMonitoringPanel`. Complementary: `/dashboard/ip-management/slots`. Overlays: `IpOverlayDialog`. Visual scope: `.ip-target`.

## Complementary vs competing

| Surface | Treat as |
|---|---|
| IP OT + slots | **Canonical production** |
| Counsellor `ScheduleSurgeryModal` / `FinalizeOtModal` | Upstream counselling handoff — do not replace the OT board |
| `/admin/inventory/surgery` | OT consumables/inventory, not the surgical board |
| Appointment FullCalendar | Clinic appointments, not IP OT |
| `/dashboard/operations/ot*`, `/dashboard/surgery-schedule` | Legacy/mock — do not extend as the OT product; do not delete without an approved nav plan |

## Must not duplicate

OT state and surgical workflow must not be reimplemented inside Billing or Coverage. Implant/IOL clinical capture stays OT/IP; charging stays Billing; payer rules stay CCMS.

## Safety

Safety checklist, implant mismatch, and anaesthesia panels are clinical-safety surfaces: no silent discards, explicit overrides where the domain already has them, permissions (e.g. `ot.safety.sign`) enforced, audit preserved. Failed scans/integrations must not look successful.
